[s0l0!-header][h1]The else Statement[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Right, so we’ve seen that the action gets skipped when a code block using the if statement evaluates to false, but what if we want something else to happen. 
Well, we use the "else" statement, of course!

We can use the [b]else [/b]statement to specify a block of code that will execute if the condition is [b]false[/b]. Like this:[code format="js" ]if (expression) {
   // executed if condition is true
}
[b]else [/b]{
   // executed if condition is false
}[/code]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
You can skip the curly braces if the code under the condition contains only one command.[/note]

