resolved.description:
[s0l0!-header][h1]The else Statement [/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Here’s another example of the [b]if [/b]and [b]else [/b]statements working together:[code format="js" codeId="4860"]var myNum1 = 7;
var myNum2 = 10;
if (myNum1 > myNum2) {
   alert("This is my first condition");
}
else {
   alert("This is my second condition");
}[/code]
Let's translate that example. It says:
- [b]If [/b]myNum1 is greater than myNum2, alert "This is my first condition";
- [b]Else[/b], alert "This is my second condition".

So the browser will print out the second condition, as 7 is not greater than 10.[img id="2752" width="100%"]
[note][b]Heads up![/b]
There's another way to do this check using the ? operator: a > b ? alert(a) : alert(b).[/note]
